          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notation “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ⟵
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}^1
            ” is common notation for the first
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mn 1
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ⟵
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^1 \underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            functor.
          %p
            Here we consider the case of limits over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+diagrams"} sequential diagrams
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            (prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Lim1IsDerivedLimit"}
            below). In good cases, this is the only obstruction to a naive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            of homotopy sets being the homotopy classes of the correct
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact
            %em Milnor sequence
            (
            %a{:href => "#MilnorSequences"}> below
            ).
          %h2#Definition Definition
          #TheBoundaryMapDefiningLim1.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tower"} tower
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\bullet
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 3
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \to A_3 \stackrel{f_2}{\to} A_2 \stackrel{f_1}{\to} A_1 \stackrel{f_0}{\to} A_0
            %p write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
