                    (a_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
                    \\mapsto
                    (a_n - f_n(a_{n+1}))_{n \in \mathbb{N}}.
          #LimitAsKernelAnalogousToLim1.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              of a sequence as in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheBoundaryMapDefiningLim1"}
              – hence the group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
                        %mo ⟵
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\longleftarrow}{\lim}_n A_n
              universally equipped with morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mi lim
